        "message": "LU-20238 ec: tighten GFNI configure probe, doc fixes\n\nThe configure GFNI probe used a static function that -O2 drops\nbefore target codegen, so it passed even without GFNI support in\nthe target attribute. Make the probe functions non-static, and add\nan AVX-512 probe that uses the {1to8} inline asm the AVX-512\nkernels need, so the assembler is checked too.\n\nAlso fix comments from the review of \"LU-20238 ec: GFNI-accelerated\nEC primitives\": the base tables are nibble-product tables, not\nlog/exp; tables from ec_init_tables() and ec_init_tables_base()/\ngf_vect_mul_init() must not be mixed on a GFNI host; the\ngfni_ec_test checklist now matches what it checks; and\ngf_vect_dot_prod()/gf_vect_mad() need kernel_fpu_begin() before\nGFNI dispatch is enabled in the kernel.\n\ngfni_ec_test now fills its test data with a local xorshift32\ninstead of rand(), which Coverity flags (CID 293327), and takes\n-s/--seed so a failing run can be repeated.\n\nsanity-ec test_0 now forces m=5 and len=4065, so the 5-vect AVX-512\nkernels and the AVX2 32B block run on every host with GFNI.  It\nalso passes a seed to each run and prints it with the result.\n\nFixes: e477182c6337 (\"LU-20238 ec: GFNI-accelerated EC primitives\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I9fa925ce52ba8d983d98fa53513a332272ee0eda\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
